litedit is an original program, written from scratch in Rust. It contains
no source code from lite-xl (https://github.com/lite-xl/lite-xl), a separate
editor written in C and Lua.

lite-xl was used as a design reference, and these specific values were
taken from it:

- the default dark colour scheme (colour values from lite-xl's
  data/colors/default.lua)
- default sizes and spacing (padding and font sizes)
- the characters that end a word, for double-click and Ctrl+arrow
- the file and folder names the file tree hides by default, such as .git

Its general design (the window layout, how editing and undo behave, fuzzy
file search) also inspired litedit's own implementation.

